      "train_qid": "26989",
      "hint": "Main trap: do not assume a random process makes all orderings equally likely, and do not jump to 1/n or 1/n!. Uniformity must be derived, never asserted. A branch is 1/2 only where two moves are genuinely available and becomes 1 once the choice is forced, so paths carry unequal weight and shorter paths are often likelier.\n\nInstead fix a compact state (the ordered contents of each pile), enumerate reachable states, multiply the actual branch probability along each path, then add the probabilities of every distinct path reaching the target event. Sanity-check that probabilities over all outcomes sum to 1, and test the same reasoning on 2 or 3 items by hand. Handle each part as a separate event, state each result in order at the end, and if you claim an outcome is impossible, name the blocking constraint.",
